Id: ssh016w
Severity: WARN
Category: ssh
Check: check_ssh
Fix: Set LogLevel VERBOSE (or INFO).
References: sshd_config(5); CIS Ubuntu Linux 24.04 LTS Benchmark v2.0.0, 5.1.14 (Ensure sshd LogLevel is configured)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 5.4; NIST AC-17, IA-2; ISO 8.5, 8.20; CE Secure configuration, User access control

LogLevel is QUIET, FATAL or ERROR, so successful and failed logins are
not logged in enough detail to investigate an incident. CIS allows INFO
(the default) or VERBOSE, which adds the fingerprint of the key each
login used: set VERBOSE where keys are in use. Lynis marks INFO down;
Tigris follows the benchmark. A DEBUG level is ssh030w.
